# Stale copies of the game have been committed twice now - game/index-1.html,
# game/index_2.html and "Claude outputs/index.html" - and each time the next
# session could not tell which file was the live one. The sail-flutter work sat
# unshipped in index_2.html for a day because of it. There is exactly one game
# file: game/index.html. The root index.html is the Pages redirect and stays.
game/index-*.html
game/index_*.html
# A quoted pattern does NOT work - git reads the quotes as literal characters, so
# "Claude outputs/*.html" has never matched anything since the day it was added.
# The whole folder is a scratch dump for files handed back during a session and
# nothing in it is part of the game, so the whole folder goes.
Claude outputs/

# Deploy scratch. The commit message used to be written to game/commitmsg.txt,
# which left the working tree permanently dirty with an untracked file after
# every single deploy. It is staged outside the repo now; this line covers the
# copies already sitting in working trees.
game/commitmsg.txt

# Deploy scratch that lands at the REPO ROOT. The rule above only covered
# game/commitmsg.txt, and the commit message for 2026-09-29b was written to
# COMMITMSG.txt at the root instead - same flattened-workspace mistake as
# HANDOFF 4.44 - so it sat untracked through two deploys.
COMMITMSG*.txt

# Probe output from the headless Blender runs: a throwaway mesh and the script
# that made it, both regenerated every time an asset is built.
blender/_probe.*
